Guard the GL_OES_standard_derivatives extension request with __VERSION__ < 300.

On PSC's PowerVR Rogue GE8300 (GLES 3.2), gl_glsl_compile_shader rewrites
the macro's "#version 130" header to "#version 300 es". Derivatives are
core in GLSL ES 3.0+, and Imagination's compiler hard-errors on the
now-meaningless OES extension declaration with an opaque "Compile failed.",
which kills the XMB ribbon fragment shader (program #62) and crashes RA
with "[GL] GL: Invalid value" → "Cannot open video driver".

Wrapping the #extension line in `#if __VERSION__ < 300` keeps the GLES 2.0
fallback intact (where the extension IS required for dFdx/dFdy) while
letting GLES 3.0+ drivers compile the shader as plain core ES.

diff --git a/gfx/drivers/gl_shaders/shaders_common.h b/gfx/drivers/gl_shaders/shaders_common.h
--- a/gfx/drivers/gl_shaders/shaders_common.h
+++ b/gfx/drivers/gl_shaders/shaders_common.h
@@ -14,7 +14,9 @@
                   "  precision mediump float;\n" \
                   "#endif\n" #src
 #define GLSL_STANDARD_DERIVATIVES(src) "#version 130\n" \
+                  "#if __VERSION__ < 300\n" \
                   "#extension GL_OES_standard_derivatives : enable\n" \
+                  "#endif\n" \
                   "#ifdef GL_ES\n" \
                   "  #ifdef GL_FRAGMENT_PRECISION_HIGH\n" \
                   "    precision highp float;\n" \
